    "title": "Tree canopy height : 2021",
    "description": "Tree canopy height map for India. Tree canopy height layer describes how tall are trees in a given pixel. \n\nThe Pan India map (except ACZ 12-15)  is available from 2017 onwards at 25m resolution. These are the classes in the current version of the map: \n1. Short \n2. Medium\n3. Tall\n\nDetails of methodology can be found in the technical manual and the codebase on [github](https://github.com/core-stack-org/core-stack-backend/tree/main/computing/tree_health).",
